---
to: ".terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.txt"
skip_empty: false
unless_exists: true
for_each: results
sparql:
  results: |
    PREFIX tv: <https://ggen.io/ontology/xaas-terraform-validate#>
    SELECT ?moduleName ?domainModule ?terraformModulePath WHERE {
      ?t a tv:ValidateTarget ;
         tv:moduleName ?moduleName ;
         tv:domainModule ?domainModule ;
         tv:terraformModulePath ?terraformModulePath .
    }
sh_after: "terraform -chdir={{ terraformModulePath }} fmt -check -diff 2>&1 | tee -a .terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.tf.log; terraform -chdir={{ terraformModulePath }} validate 2>&1 | tee -a .terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.tf.log"
---
real terraform fmt -check / validate invocation, driven by the live tv:ValidateTarget
ontology row {{ moduleName }} (same SPARQL -> for_each -> sh_after pattern already
proven for Ash codegen in templates-hooks/ash-gen-resource.txt.tmpl), scoped to
{{ terraformModulePath }}/ -- the module path is now ontology-driven, not hardcoded,
so this one template validates every tv:ValidateTarget row, not just one module.
generated: {{ moduleName }}
domain: {{ domainModule }}
path: {{ terraformModulePath }}
command: terraform -chdir={{ terraformModulePath }} fmt -check -diff
command: terraform -chdir={{ terraformModulePath }} validate

Deliberately non-mutating: `fmt -check` and `validate` only read/lint the real
.tf files under that module -- no `terraform apply`/`plan` against live state,
since apply would create real GitHub resources unpredictably from a research task.
